{"timestamp":"00:02:20.507","source":"Browser","level":"LOG","message":"{\"discipline\":\"Doctor\",\"environment\":\"Calendar\",\"manual\":\"**Title:**  \\nManaging File Transfers and Accessing Visual Studio Code in the Calendar Software\\n\\n**Purpose:**  \\nThis instruction guides healthcare professionals on how to monitor large file transfers and how to access Visual Studio Code within the software environment, ensuring effective use of the tools provided.\\n\\n**Prerequisites:**  \\n- Access to the enterprise calendar software.  \\n- Proper permissions to view ongoing transfers and launch Visual Studio Code.  \\n\\n**Procedure:**  \\n\\n1. **Monitoring File Transfer Progress:**  \\n- Observe the progress bar indicating the transfer of files named “Moving 164,345 files to ‘Documents’.”  \\n- Note the current transfer details:  \\n  - Files transferred: 164,147 out of 164,345.  \\n  - Estimated time remaining: approximately 18 seconds.  \\n  - Transfer speed: 45.8 MB/s.  \\n\\n2. **Accessing Visual Studio Code:**  \\n- Locate and open the calendar environment.  \\n- In the main interface, find and select the “Welcome” tab.  \\n- From the list of options, click on “Open File...” to access Visual Studio Code.  \\n- The Visual Studio Code window will open, showing the “Edit evolved” status and default start options such as creating a “New File,” opening an existing file, or opening a folder.  \\n\\n**Tips:**  \\n- During large file transfers, ensure your system remains stable and do not interrupt the process.  \\n- Use the “Open File...” option in the welcome screen for quick access to Visual Studio Code.  \\n\\n**FAQ:**  \\n- **Q:** Can I pause the file transfer?  \\n  - **A:** The screenshots do not show an option to pause or cancel the transfer.  \\n- **Q:** How do I know when the transfer is complete?  \\n  - **A:** When the progress bar reaches 100% and indicates the last file was transferred, the process is complete.  \\n- **Q:** How do I open an existing file in Visual Studio Code?  \\n  - **A:** Click “Open File...” after launching Visual Studio Code from the welcome screen.\",\"screenshots\":[\"Screenshot From 2026-06-30 23-03-42.png\",\"Screenshot From 2026-07-06 19-07-35.png\"],\"status\":\"success\"}"}
