{"timestamp":"00:17:21.965","source":"Browser","level":"LOG","message":"{\"discipline\":\"Doctor\",\"environment\":\"Planning wizard\",\"manual\":\"# Work Instruction: Moving Files in Planning Wizard\\n\\n# Purpose\\nThis procedure details the steps to move a large number of files within the Planning Wizard software environment.\\n\\n# Prerequisites\\n- The Planning Wizard application must be open and visible on the screen.\\n\\n# Procedure\\n1. Observe the transfer process in progress:\\n   - Look at the progress bar indicating the transfer of 164,345 files.\\n   - Confirm the source folder labeled \\\"Julia 1TB\\\" and the transfer status.\\n2. Once the transfer completes, review the confirmation:\\n   - The progress bar shows \\\"Moving 164,345 files to 'Documents'.\\\"\\n   - The transfer has processed 164,147 out of 164,345 files, with approximately 18 seconds remaining.\\n3. Open Visual Studio Code:\\n   - Locate the \\\"Welcome\\\" tab, which is open by default.\\n   - The interface shows options to create a new file, open a file, open a folder, clone a git repository, connect to, or generate a new workspace.\\n\\n# Tips\\n- No additional tips available.\\n\\n# FAQ\\nQ1: How many files are being moved?\\n- 164,345 files.\\n\\nQ2: What is the target folder for the move?\\n- The files are moving to the \\\"Documents\\\" folder.\\n\\nQ3: How much time is estimated for the transfer to complete?\\n- About 18 seconds remaining.\",\"screenshots\":[\"Screenshot From 2026-06-30 23-03-42.png\",\"Screenshot From 2026-07-06 19-07-35.png\"],\"status\":\"success\"}"}
