{"timestamp":"00:19:25.190","source":"Browser","level":"LOG","message":"{\"discipline\":\"Doctor\",\"environment\":\"Planning wizard\",\"manual\":\"# Work Instruction: Moving Files in Planning Wizard and Accessing Visual Studio Code\\n\\n# Purpose\\nTo guide the user through transferring files within the Planning Wizard application and opening Visual Studio Code.\\n\\n# Prerequisites\\n- None visible.\\n\\n# Procedure\\n\\n1. Initiate File Transfer in Planning Wizard\\n   - Observe the progress bar indicating files are being moved from \\\"Julia 1TB\\\" to \\\"Documents\\\" (Screenshot 1).\\n   - Wait until the transfer completes, as shown by the progress bar reaching 100% and the display of total files (164,345 files) remaining the same.\\n\\n2. Confirm Transfer Completion\\n   - Observe the message indicating \\\"Moving 164,345 files to 'Documents'\\\" with details: \\\"164,147 / 164,345 — 18 seconds left (45.8 MB/s)\\\". No additional action is required.\\n\\n3. Open Visual Studio Code\\n   - Locate the Visual Studio Code application window.\\n   - Confirm the interface displays \\\"Welcome\\\" with options listed under \\\"Start\\\" and \\\"Recent\\\" (Screenshot 2).\\n\\n4. Access Working Environment\\n   - At this stage, the user has the option to create a new file, open an existing file, open a folder, clone a Git repository, connect to a remote, or generate a new workspace by clicking the respective options shown in the \\\"Start\\\" section.\\n   - Alternatively, the user can open a recent folder from the \\\"Recent\\\" section if available.\\n\\n# Tips\\n- No additional tips available.\\n\\n# FAQ\\nQ1: How do I start editing a new file?\\nA1: Click on \\\"New File...\\\" in the Welcome screen's \\\"Start\\\" section.\\n\\nQ2: How can I open an existing folder?\\nA2: Click on \\\"Open Folder...\\\" from the options listed in the \\\"Start\\\" section.\\n\\nQ3: How do I access recent folders?\\nA3: Scroll down to the \\\"Recent\\\" section and click on \\\"open a folder\\\" if available.\",\"screenshots\":[\"Screenshot From 2026-06-30 23-03-42.png\",\"Screenshot From 2026-07-06 19-07-35.png\"],\"status\":\"success\"}"}
